Error [jet.TypestateUnknownState]: `Stuffed` is not a declared state of `Crate`
  --> tests/ui/typestate_unknown_state.jet:10:19
    |
 10 |     get: fn(self: Crate.Stuffed) -> Int { return self.data }
    |                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: Typestate: `Crate: struct { state { … } }` defines the valid state labels; `Stuffed` is not among them — a typo here would silently create a phantom state that no transition reaches
 Fix: Add `Stuffed` inside `Crate: struct { state { … } }`, or correct the spelling
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0151

Error [jet.TypestateWrongState]: `get` needs `Crate.Stuffed`, but `b` is `Crate.Full`
  --> tests/ui/typestate_unknown_state.jet:15:13
    |
 15 |     print(b.get())
    |             ^^^
 Why: Typestate: `get` takes only `Crate.Stuffed`; calling it with `Crate` in another state is the out-of-order bug the state list rules out
 Fix: Bring `b` to `Crate.Stuffed` before calling `get`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0150
